The following types port behaviour observed in that project at commit
bd10fa61c1727996607593d26631f9b22bb41d14, read on 8 August 2026. Each names the
upstream class and the file the expected values were taken from, and each is
pinned by a test under io.akka.evalkit.conformance.

  io.akka.evalkit.metric.ToolPermission
      from ToolPermissionMetric
      tests/test_metrics/test_tool_permission_metric.py

  io.akka.evalkit.metric.TurnRelevancy
      from TurnRelevancyMetric
      tests/test_metrics/test_turn_relevancy_aggregation.py

  io.akka.evalkit.metric.TurnFaithfulness
      from TurnFaithfulnessMetric
      tests/test_metrics/test_turn_faithfulness_metric_empty_verdicts.py

  io.akka.evalkit.metric.CitationFaithfulness
      from CitationFaithfulnessMetric
      tests/test_metrics/test_citation_faithfulness_metric.py

  io.akka.evalkit.metric.dag.Dag
  io.akka.evalkit.metric.dag.DagNode
  io.akka.evalkit.metric.dag.DagJudge
      from DAGMetric and its node types
      tests/test_metrics/test_dag.py

io.akka.evalkit.conformance.PortedMetrics carries the same record in code, and
ConformanceCoverageTest fails the build when a ported metric appears without an
entry or an entry appears without a test.
